  "question": {
    "text": "A value of $x$ for which $\\sin \\left(\\cot ^{-1}(1+x)\\right)=\\cos$ $\\left(\\tan ^{-1} x\\right)$, is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$-\\frac{1}{2}$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n 1\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n0\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\sin \\left(\\cot ^{-1}(1+x)\\right)=\\cos \\left(\\tan ^{-1} x\\right)$\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\Rightarrow \\operatorname{cosec}^2\\left(\\cot ^{-1}(1+x)\\right)=\\sec ^2\\left(\\tan ^{-1} x\\right) \\\\ & \\Rightarrow 1+\\left[\\cot \\left(\\cot ^{-1}(1+x)\\right)\\right]^2 \\\\ & \\Rightarrow=1+\\left[\\sec \\left(\\tan ^{-1} x\\right)\\right]^2 \\\\ & \\Rightarrow(1+x)^2=x^2 \\Rightarrow x=-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}